Contradictions may be explicit or implicit. A triple is valid if, given normal world knowledge and ontological constraints (e.g., role exclusivity, type incompatibility, identity constraints), it makes at least one input triple impossible to be true. Do not reject a triple merely because the contradiction is not stated verbatim in the text.

Every provided contradicting triple must individually contradict the input. If any triple does not create a real contradiction, the overall answer must be judged incorrect.

Do the labels of entities and predicates used in the contradicted triples correctly correspond to their identifiers?
Note that negating predicates ("not located in") or entities ("not Boston") is not allowed.

To verify condition 2, use the functions available to retrieve labels for identifiers mentioned in the contradicting triples.

